<title>MEXICO: Mexico applies U.S. bacon import quota, tariff.</title>
<headline>Mexico applies U.S. bacon import quota, tariff.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Trade Ministry said Tuesday it had activated a safeguard under the North American Trade Agreement (NAFTA) and set a quota for streaky bacon imports from the United States.</p>
<p>The import quota has been set at 3,605 tonnes for sides of streaky bacon and bacon parts at a preferential tariff of 6 percent, the ministry said.</p>
<p>&quot;Once this quota has been reached, imports of streaky bacon will have to pay a tariff of 10 percent from the publication of this safeguard to December 31, 1997,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>The ministry did not give a breakdown of streaky bacon imports to date.</p>
<p>&quot;This safeguard measure is to regulate streaky bacon imports and to prevent damage to the national bacon industry...&quot; the ministry added.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530))</p>
